MiSTer text in the Tango authors' files
---------------------------------------
  - rtl/tango_core_arcade_template.v, both CONF_STR variants: the entries "T[0],Reset;" and "R[0],Reset and close
    OSD;", as in Template_MiSTer's Template.sv (https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Template_MiSTer; its header: GNU
    General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version), the entries most MiSTer cores carry.
  - rtl/tango_core_arcade_template.v, comments: quotes of two CONF_STR lines of Arcade-Galaga_MiSTer's
    Arcade-Galaga.sv, "J1,Fire,Start 1P,Start 2P,Coin,Pause;" and "jn,A,Start,Select,R,L;"
    (https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Arcade-Galaga_MiSTer; the file's header: "Port to MiSTer", "Copyright (C) 2017
    Sorgelig", GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version).
  - fixtures/Arcade Template Test.mra, a comment: a quote of the <buttons> line of MiSTer's Galaxian .mra,
    <buttons default="A,Start,Select,R,B,L" names="Fire,Start 1P,Start 2P,Coin,Test,Pause">, as an example of
    MiSTer's per-game button override.


Following other projects' behaviour
-----------------------------------
These files are the Tango authors' code (GPL-2.0-or-later); they follow documented or observed behaviour of other
projects, which they cite:
  - The menu string format (CONF_STR, with its "DIP" and "J1" entries) and the core interface are MiSTer's
    (sys-tango's NOTICE); the .mra format of fixtures/Arcade Template Test.mra is MiSTer's arcade ROM description.
  - rtl/tango_core_arcade_template.v: the joystick bit order and the button-name mapping of Main_MiSTer (input.h,
    joymapping.cpp), as the comments cite them; the native 288 x 224 raster (384 x 264 total) is Galaga's video
    timing as Arcade-Galaga_MiSTer's rtl/gen_video.vhd has it.


ROMs: none.  The .mra fixture's only ROM part is 16 bytes written inline in the file, the ASCII text
"TANGO-A5-ROM-OK!".
